// The pointer's shape (Pointer-Affordances.md §4). Elements carry
// `data-pointer` from the one shared function (`common/pointer_shape`,
// stamped by `ui/pointer_stamp`), and these are the only `cursor` rules in the
// stylesheets. During a gesture the body carries `data-pointer-gesture`, which
// wins over every element until the gesture ends.
for shape in default pointer text col-resize row-resize grab grabbing not-allowed
  [data-pointer=\"{shape}\"]
    cursor: unquote(shape)
  body[data-pointer-gesture=\"{shape}\"],
  body[data-pointer-gesture=\"{shape}\"] *
    cursor: unquote(shape) !important

// A divider's drag handle is the part of the divider the pointer actually
// rests on. GoldenLayout's own stylesheet gives it `ew-resize` / `ns-resize`,
// which covered the shape the divider is stamped with (`col-resize` /
// `row-resize`, `ui/pointer_stamp.nim`): it takes its divider's shape instead.
// It is here, not in golden_layout.styl, because this sheet is the only one
// that may say `cursor` (PA-1; test_plat70f_pointer_shapes.nim's source gate).
.lm_splitter .lm_drag_handle
  cursor: inherit !important
